"evidence\": \"Nimbrel Relay stalls\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists this as a consequence of append requests returning 429.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-003\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"batch loaders resend the same envelope\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists this as a consequence of append requests returning 429.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-004\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reads against the same shard begin to time out\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists this as a consequence of append requests returning 429.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-005\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The refusal reaches the client and is written to the Relay and Collector logs as well.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-006\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Every Nimbrel Ledger release on every platform can refuse an append this way.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this claim about universal platform and release coverage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-007\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A [`429 - Too Many Requests` reply](https://docs.nimbrel.example/ledger/http-status-codes) is what a Ledger node sends once it has nowhere left to put the work, which is to say once [an append queue or a read queue is full](https://docs.nimbrel.example/ledger/why-appends-are-refused).\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states this equivalence, supporting the claim through the 'which is to say' connector.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-008\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The `append` or `system_append` worker pools hold more batches than they have slots for\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists this as the first of three ways an append draws a 429.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The ingest memory guard has refused the batch\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists this as the second of three ways an append draws a 429.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A circuit breaker has tripped\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text lists this as the third of three ways an append draws a 429.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a breaker trips on any operation and is not particular to appends.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this characteristic of circuit breakers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"From release 4.6 and release 5.1 onward, appending to a `wide_text` column draws a 429 on its own account whenever the batch would otherwise have run the node out of memory.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this release-specific behavior for wide_text columns.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-013\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A cluster that refuses appends has been given more work than its hardware can carry\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this diagnosis in the Resolution section.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-014\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Splitting a hot stream over more leader shards spreads append load across more nodes, which helps in some layouts.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this optimization approach.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-015\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the `ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling` cluster setting, which defaults to 10% of the heap.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text explicitly states this default value for the setting.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-016\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A higher ceiling lets a node hold more in-flight append memory before refusing\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this effect of raising the ceiling.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-017\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a node holding too much runs out of memory instead of refusing\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this consequence of excessive in-flight append memory.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-018\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The setting is read at startup\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states when the ingest_guard.memory.leader.ceiling setting is read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-019\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the cluster must be restarted for a change to take.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states that cluster restart is required for setting changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"A-020\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Refusals that show up only during a spike usually clear on their own once the queues drain.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this behavior for spike-related refusals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-001\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text describes general append refusal behavior and does not describe a specific managed deployment's metrics over a fortnight.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-002\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Nimbrel Ledger\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The entire reference document establishes Nimbrel Ledger as the product being discussed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-003\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text mentions releases 4.6 and 5.1 and states every release can refuse appends, but does not describe a specific case or deployment as version 4.4 or 5.x.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-004\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text states the issue affects every platform but does not identify Nimbrel Cloud specifically.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-005\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not mention Managed Ledger Service or specific deployment types.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-006\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not specify whether the case described is production or another environment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-007\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not describe a specific managed deployment or its growing share of 429 replies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-008\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not compare or validate front proxy counters against client reports.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-009\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text does not address whether observed refusals are real or client-side accounting errors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-010\",\n      \"verdict\": \"MISSING\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text mentions queries running for several seconds but does not specifically state that a handful run for 2 seconds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-011\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A query that runs for several seconds holds a worker slot unavailable for other work\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text supports that a worker slot is unavailable for the duration a query holds it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-012\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"evidence\": \"and the queue behind it grows.\",\n      \"evidence_source\": \"merged.md\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The reference text directly states this consequence in the context of slow queries.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"B-013\",\n      \"verdict\": 